#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-operationaldb.md
msgid "CAP-OPERATIONALDB Operational database with branching"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-operationaldb.md
msgid "Each product's transactional Postgres store, with copy-on-write branches of production."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-operationaldb.md
msgid "Layer L1 · domain: data · depends on: [CAP-IDENTITY]{1}."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-operationaldb.md
msgid "Purpose"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-operationaldb.md
msgid "Each product gets a transactional Postgres database that can be branched for development and testing."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-operationaldb.md
msgid "Why"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-operationaldb.md
msgid "Branching gives every change a full copy of production without the cost of copying it ([P6]{1}, [P7]{2}). There are two gatekeepers, the catalog's policies and the database's policies, and they have to agree, so each is set up together with the other."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-operationaldb.md
msgid "Interfaces"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-operationaldb.md
msgid "The Postgres wire protocol and SQL."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-operationaldb.md
msgid "Branches that expire after a set time, and a protected production branch."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-operationaldb.md
msgid "A role for each identity, and row-level security."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-operationaldb.md
msgid "A migration ledger, and a schema check inside the application."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-operationaldb.md
msgid "Notes"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-operationaldb.md
msgid "If row-level security doesn't admit a database role, that role reads zero rows, without any error. When the catalog reads an operational database, test that its identity is admitted before you rely on it."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-operationaldb.md
msgid "Contract"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-operationaldb.md
msgid "Clause"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-operationaldb.md
msgid "Level"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-operationaldb.md
msgid "Requirement"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-operationaldb.md
msgid "How conformance is shown"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-operationaldb.md
msgid "CAP-OPERATIONALDB.1"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-operationaldb.md
msgid "MUST"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-operationaldb.md
msgid "The operational database speaks the Postgres protocol and SQL dialect."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-operationaldb.md
msgid "The product's migrations and tests run unchanged against it."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-operationaldb.md
msgid "CAP-OPERATIONALDB.2"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-operationaldb.md
msgid "A branch of production, or of a point in time, is created without copying data first, and carries a time to live.{1}*Example:* A developer branches production as it was at 09:00 to test a migration; the branch costs nothing until it diverges and is deleted automatically after seven days."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-operationaldb.md
msgid "Create a branch of the production database and time it; it expires on schedule."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-operationaldb.md
msgid "CAP-OPERATIONALDB.3"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-operationaldb.md
msgid "The production branch is protected from deletion and from writes by development identities."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-operationaldb.md
msgid "Negative tests: delete and write as a development identity both fail."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-operationaldb.md
msgid "CAP-OPERATIONALDB.4"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-operationaldb.md
msgid "Connections authenticate per identity; an application's access is governed by database roles and row-level security, and each catalog policy names its database counterpart or states there is none."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-operationaldb.md
msgid "No shared password role is in use; the policy register pairs each catalog policy with its database policy."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-operationaldb.md
msgid "CAP-OPERATIONALDB.5"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-operationaldb.md
msgid "Migrations are idempotent twice over: a ledger records what ran, and every statement can be run again safely. Schemas change by expand then contract, one phase per migration, and the application refuses to write to a database behind its code.{1}*Example:* A migration that adds a column is run twice on a branch in CI; the second run changes nothing, and the application refuses to write to a database still on the previous schema."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-operationaldb.md
msgid "CI applies every migration twice to a branch; the application's schema gate is tested against an older database."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-operationaldb.md
msgid "CAP-OPERATIONALDB.6"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-operationaldb.md
msgid "Committed records survive loss of a node (recovery point zero), and the database can be restored to a point in time."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-operationaldb.md
msgid "Restore drill to a point in time, comparing per-table content hashes."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-operationaldb.md
msgid "CAP-OPERATIONALDB.7"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-operationaldb.md
msgid "SHOULD"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-operationaldb.md
msgid "Analytics read operational data through the catalog or a governed extract, never through a direct connection."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-operationaldb.md
msgid "No analytics identity holds a database login."
msgstr ""

